The '''Lutrillian Cross''' was a [[hyperspace route]] that joined [[Mijos]] and [[Lutrillia]].<ref name="BMF 18" /> At Lutrillia, the route met the endpoints of the [[Cerean Reach]]<ref name="Cerea">{{EncyclopediaCite|Bespin and Other Planets in the Outer Rim}}</ref> and the [[Koda Spur]].<ref name="Koda">{{GalaxyMapHyperlanes|route=Koda Spur|canon={{EncyclopediaCite|Scarif and Other Planets in the Outer Rim}}|leg=''[[The Essential Atlas]]''}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The Lutrillian Cross was first mentioned in the new ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in the [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 18|eighteenth issue]] of [[De Agostini]]'s ''[[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon]]'' magazine,<ref name="BMF 18" /> published around [[May 6]], [[2015]].<ref name="BMFdate">{{BuildFalconDates|18}}</ref> In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, the [[Lutrillian Cross/Legends|Lutrillian Cross]] was introduced in "[[Galactic Gazetteer: Hoth and the Greater Javin]]," an article published by [[Wizards of the Coast]] for the ''[[Star Wars Roleplaying Game]]'' on [[Wizards.com]] on [[March 25]], [[2004]].<ref name="Gazetteer">{{Wizards|url=default.asp?x=starwars/article/sw20040325web|text=Galactic Gazetteer: Hoth and the Greater Javin|int=Galactic Gazetteer: Hoth and the Greater Javin}}</ref>

The [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 62|sixty-second issue]] of the ''Build the Millennium Falcon'' series incorrectly placed [[Lotho Minor]] on the Lutrillian Cross,<ref name="BMF 62">{{BuildFalconCite|62|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> when in actuality it falls on he [[Koda Spur]].<ref name="Koda" />

